{#
  Home. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md `/`. Design: DESIGN_SYSTEM.md v2 and
  _reference/tajima-home-v2.html, the client-approved reference implementation.

  SEVEN SECTIONS: hero, intro, trio, statement, bowls, locations field, then
  the neon block and footer from the layout. The reference file also carries
  `craft` and `feed` sections. Both were rejected in review after the client
  saw them and were simply never deleted from the prototype, so they are not
  built here. DESIGN_SYSTEM.md "Page composition" is right and the file is
  stale on that one point.

  COPY IS THE REFERENCE'S, VERBATIM, WITH ONE DELETION. The trio's broth card
  read "Tonkotsu simmered twelve hours in our Crown Point kitchen". No simmer
  time is confirmed anywhere in CLIENT_FACTS.md, and site.json `_specNote`
  already records this exact number being cut once before as invented. The
  number is dropped; the rest of the sentence stands. Do not put it back
  without a source.

  Everything else was checked against CLIENT_FACTS.md before shipping: Sam
  taking over the Convoy Street restaurant in 2001 and it already being called
  Tajima (:383), two years building the room (:173, and the press line at
  :357), the machine from Japan and the two noodle types (:259, :385), broth
  made every morning and driven to the San Diego locations (:385), walk-in
  with no reservations (:236).

  REQUIRED INTERNAL LINKS, per the brief: /noodle-room/ in body prose (the
  intro, not just the statement button), /menu/, /locations/, all seven
  location pages, /about/.
#}

{% include "components/icon-sprite.njk" %}

{# ============================== HERO ==============================
   Brand guidelines p19: full-bleed video, logo lockup centred, slogan
   beneath. No nav overlay, no stat bar, nothing else in frame.

   The video is decorative and carries the story; it is muted, looping and
   aria-hidden. No `heroImage` preload in front matter, because the LCP
   element here is the logo, which is already a small PNG, and preloading the
   video would compete with it. #}
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <video
    class="hero__media"
    src="https://cdn.circulationstudio.com/tajima-temp/videos/tajima-san-diego-web-background-full.mp4"
    autoplay
    muted
    loop
    playsinline
    preload="metadata"
    aria-hidden="true"></video>

  <div class="hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="hero__mark">
    <div class="hero__lockup">
      {# The dark-surface lockup regardless of theme: this sits on video, not
         on the page canvas, so it does not follow data-mode. #}
      <img
        class="hero__logo"
        src="/images/brand/tajima-logo-header-dark.png"
        alt="{{ site.logo.alt }}"
        width="800"
        height="356"
        fetchpriority="high">

      {# The one h1. Exact string, per DESIGN_SYSTEM.md "Copy constants":
         "Housemade" is one word with no hyphen. From site.json. #}
      <h1 class="hero__slogan" id="hero-title">
        {{ site.slogan.before }}<em>{{ site.slogan.emphasis }}</em>
      </h1>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="hero__cue" aria-hidden="true"><span></span>Since {{ site.founded }}</p>
</section>

{# ============================== INTRO ============================== #}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="intro-t">
  <div class="sect__in intro reveal">
    <div>
      <h2 class="h2" id="intro-t">A ramen house that makes <em>its own noodles.</em></h2>

      {# The brief requires /noodle-room/ as an in-body prose link, not just a
         button. It is the growth priority. #}
      <p class="lede">
        Sam Morikizono took over a small restaurant on Convoy Street in {{ site.founded }}.
        It was already called Tajima. Twenty-five years later the noodles are cut in
        <a class="link" href="/noodle-room/">our own room in Crown Point</a>, and the broth is
        simmered there every morning before service.
      </p>

      <p class="lede">
        <a class="link" href="/about/">Read the story</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="intro__photo">
      <img
        src="{{ photos.photos['tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-03.webp'].src }}"
        alt="{{ photos.photos['tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-03.webp'].alt }}"
        width="{{ photos.photos['tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-03.webp'].width }}"
        height="{{ photos.photos['tajima-ramen-convoy-traditonal-tonkotsu-03.webp'].height }}"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async">
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================== TRIO ============================== #}
<section class="sect sect--alt" aria-labelledby="trio-t">
  <div class="sect__in">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2 class="h2" id="trio-t">Three things we <em>don't buy in.</em></h2>
    </div>

    <div class="trio">
      <article class="card reveal">
        <div class="card__ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-noodle-wordmark"></use></svg></div>
        <h3 class="card__t">The noodles</h3>
        <p class="card__b">Cut daily in the Noodle Room on a machine brought over from Japan. Two kinds so far, including the spinach noodle for the vegan bowl.</p>
      </article>

      {# "twelve hours" deleted from this sentence. See the note at the top of
         this file: no simmer time is confirmed in CLIENT_FACTS.md. #}
      <article class="card reveal">
        <div class="card__ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-broth-pot"></use></svg></div>
        <h3 class="card__t">The broth</h3>
        <p class="card__b">Tonkotsu simmered in our Crown Point kitchen, then driven to every San Diego location before service.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="card reveal">
        <div class="card__ico"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-chopsticks-noodles"></use></svg></div>
        <h3 class="card__t">The bowl</h3>
        <p class="card__b">Tajima Red, Black, and White. Spicy Sesame. Chicken, Miso, Vegan. Built the same way in all six rooms.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================ STATEMENT ============================
   Full-bleed photo, display-scale line, one CTA. The scrim and the text
   shadows are load-bearing for legibility, not decoration.

   The reference points this at an "Offsite Kitchen" frame that has no local
   copy. Substituted with the commissary steam-tank photograph, which is the
   same subject and is the only commissary frame carrying reviewed alt text.
   Its photos.json entry is proposedUseLocked, so this placement is a decision
   on the record, not a rename. #}
<section class="stmt" aria-labelledby="stmt-t">
  <img
    class="stmt__media"
    src="{{ photos.photos['tajima-commissary-steam-tanks-02-landscape.webp'].src }}"
    alt="{{ photos.photos['tajima-commissary-steam-tanks-02-landscape.webp'].alt }}"
    width="{{ photos.photos['tajima-commissary-steam-tanks-02-landscape.webp'].width }}"
    height="{{ photos.photos['tajima-commissary-steam-tanks-02-landscape.webp'].height }}"
    loading="lazy"
    decoding="async">

  <div class="stmt__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="stmt__in reveal">
    <h2 class="stmt__line" id="stmt-t">Better noodles weren't for sale. <em>So we made them.</em></h2>
    <p class="stmt__sub">Two years building the room. A lifetime building the bowl.</p>
    <p class="stmt__cta">
      <a class="btn" href="/noodle-room/">Inside the Noodle Room
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M1 7h12M13 7l-5.5-5.5M13 7l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{# ============================== BOWLS ==============================
   Exactly three. The house trio is Red, Black, White; Spicy Sesame is not
   part of it.

   NO PRICES. menu.json carries 17.50 for all three, but its own _priceStatus
   records that figure as stale and wrong for every location: Convoy is 18.00,
   Plaza Bonita 16.00, Maui 20.00 to 21.00. One brand price cannot be right
   for seven rooms, so the tiles carry the name and link to /menu/. #}
<section class="sect" aria-labelledby="bowls-t">
  <div class="sect__in">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2 class="h2" id="bowls-t">The house <em>trio.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">One tonkotsu base, three finishes. Red for heat, Black for garlic, White for the broth itself.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bowls">
      {%- set trio = ["tajima-ramen-convoy-tajima-red-01.webp", "tajima-ramen-convoy-tajima-black-03.webp", "tajima-ramen-convoy-tajima-white-01.webp"] %}
      {%- set trioNames = ["Tajima Red", "Tajima Black", "Tajima White"] %}
      {%- for file in trio %}
        {%- set photo = photos.photos[file] %}
        <a class="bowl reveal" href="/menu/">
          <img
            class="bowl__img"
            src="{{ photo.src }}"
            alt="{{ photo.alt }}"
            width="{{ photo.width }}"
            height="{{ photo.height }}"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async">
          <span class="bowl__cap"><span class="bowl__name">{{ trioNames[loop.index0] }}</span></span>
        </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{# =========================== LOCATIONS ============================
   The one place red runs as a field rather than an accent.

   THE PATTERN IS INDIVIDUALLY POSITIONED ELEMENTS, NOT A REPEATING <pattern>.
   A <pattern> renders every tile identically, cannot animate per icon, and
   failed to span full width. Each icon carries its own rotation, duration and
   delay so nothing pulses in unison. Do not convert this to a pattern fill.

   Icons come through the sprite as <use>, so eighteen appearances cost one
   copy of the path data rather than eighteen.

   THE GRID IS THE SIX SAN DIEGO ROOMS, from locations.json by region. The
   reference hardcodes eight entries including Tijuana, which breaks two rules
   at once: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md says Tijuana is an outbound link and "not a
   card", and voice-tone.md forbids publishing a global location count. Maui
   and Tijuana sit below the grid instead, which also keeps the heading honest.
   The brief's requirement that all seven location pages be linked is still
   met, Maui included. #}
<section class="red" aria-labelledby="red-t">
  <div class="red__pattern" aria-hidden="true">
    {%- set field = [
      { i: "noodle-wordmark",     a: "a", s: "left:-4%;top:-12%;width:17rem;--rot:-10deg;--dur:21s;--delay:0.0s" },
      { i: "ramen-bowl",          a: "c", s: "left:9%;top:30%;width:20rem;--rot:5deg;--dur:25s;--delay:1.8s" },
      { i: "garlic",              a: "b", s: "left:24%;top:-14%;width:13rem;--rot:14deg;--dur:19s;--delay:0.6s" },
      { i: "chopsticks-noodles",  a: "a", s: "left:20%;top:62%;width:16rem;--rot:-8deg;--dur:23s;--delay:2.6s" },
      { i: "egg",                 a: "b", s: "left:37%;top:16%;width:15rem;--rot:7deg;--dur:27s;--delay:1.2s" },
      { i: "chili",               a: "c", s: "left:34%;top:74%;width:10rem;--rot:-22deg;--dur:17s;--delay:3.1s" },
      { i: "onigiri",             a: "a", s: "left:48%;top:52%;width:14rem;--rot:12deg;--dur:22s;--delay:0.4s" },
      { i: "naruto-small",        a: "c", s: "left:50%;top:-8%;width:10rem;--rot:0deg;--dur:24s;--delay:2.2s" },
      { i: "noodle-wordmark",     a: "b", s: "left:62%;top:30%;width:16rem;--rot:9deg;--dur:20s;--delay:1.5s" },
      { i: "steam",               a: "a", s: "left:60%;top:84%;width:8rem;--rot:0deg;--dur:16s;--delay:3.4s" },
      { i: "garlic",              a: "c", s: "left:74%;top:-6%;width:12rem;--rot:-18deg;--dur:26s;--delay:0.9s" },
      { i: "ramen-bowl",          a: "b", s: "left:78%;top:58%;width:19rem;--rot:-4deg;--dur:21s;--delay:2.9s" },
      { i: "chili",               a: "a", s: "left:90%;top:22%;width:10rem;--rot:34deg;--dur:18s;--delay:1.7s" },
      { i: "onigiri",             a: "c", s: "left:94%;top:80%;width:13rem;--rot:-7deg;--dur:25s;--delay:3.6s" },
      { i: "egg",                 a: "b", s: "left:0%;top:78%;width:14rem;--rot:-10deg;--dur:23s;--delay:2.0s" },
      { i: "naruto",              a: "a", s: "left:44%;top:-2%;width:9rem;--rot:0deg;--dur:19s;--delay:4.0s" },
      { i: "toppings",            a: "c", s: "left:28%;top:40%;width:17rem;--rot:6deg;--dur:28s;--delay:1.1s" },
      { i: "steam",               a: "b", s: "left:86%;top:46%;width:7rem;--rot:0deg;--dur:15s;--delay:2.4s" }
    ] %}
    {%- for icon in field %}
      <span class="ic ic--{{ icon.a }}" style="{{ icon.s }}"><svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><use href="#i-{{ icon.i }}"></use></svg></span>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="red__in">
    <div class="reveal">
      <h2 class="h2" id="red-t">Six rooms in San Diego. <em>Walk in.</em></h2>
      <p class="lede">No reservations. Same noodles in every bowl, cut that morning in Crown Point.</p>
    </div>

    {# Descriptors are composed from the data, never written here. Where the
       descriptor and the neighborhood are the same word (Maui is "Kihei" in
       both), one carries the line, the same fix loc-card already makes for
       Crown Point. #}
    <div class="red__grid reveal">
      {%- for loc in locations.items | where("region", "san-diego") %}
        <a class="red__loc" href="{{ loc.url }}">
          <span class="red__name">{{ loc.name }}</span>
          <span class="red__hood">
            {{- loc.descriptor }}{% if loc.neighborhood and loc.neighborhood != loc.descriptor and loc.neighborhood != loc.name %} &middot; {{ loc.neighborhood }}{% endif -%}
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>

    <div class="red__foot reveal">
      <a class="btn btn--cream" href="/locations/">All locations and hours
        <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M1 7h12M13 7l-5.5-5.5M13 7l-5.5 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    {# Maui is a Tajima room and gets a real link to its page. Tijuana is a
       separate company on a separate domain and is an outbound link, never a
       card: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md, and the same treatment /locations/ uses. #}
    {%- set maui = locations.items | where("id", "maui") | first %}
    <p class="red__beyond reveal">
      Beyond San Diego: <a href="{{ maui.url }}">{{ maui.name }}</a>, in {{ maui.descriptor }}.
      Tijuana is run separately, at <a href="https://tajimamx.com" rel="noopener">tajimamx.com</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
